Team —

Legal won't give us a clean brief this week. Below is what I told product yesterday for the early-stage, single-product dialler. Treat this as operational guidance, not marketing copy.

SCOPE
We only dial accounts that are between 1 and 45 days past due on one product. Synthetic data only for the build.

OPENING (before any debt talk)
First thing out of the agent's mouth: it is Freya Bank's digital assistant and the call is recorded. Do not say collections, debt, payment, or the product name until identity clears — that ban applies even when a relative picks up.
Then ask: Am I speaking with {title} {last_name}?
Only yes / that's me / speaking / the customer's own name count. Hello, go ahead, who is this → ask once more. Still muddy after the second ask → close with outcome not_reached reason unclear.

IF SOMEONE ELSE ANSWERS
Do not explain why we called. Ask when we can reach the customer.
Callback window: same calendar day as `now`, or the next business day; clock time from 10:00 through 19:00 inclusive; must be later than `now`. Schedule it, then close not_reached / callback.
Outside that window twice → not_reached / no_callback.
Wrong number → not_reached / wrong_number.
Customer deceased → say exactly: I am sorry for your loss. Then not_reached / deceased. Nothing else.

IDENTITY
Two questions, in this order: (1) date of birth, (2) last four digits of the phone on file.
Pipe answers through verify_identity. DOB must go as YYYY-MM-DD; if they give only numbers, read day then month then year.
Three wrong answers total and we're done → not_verified / failed. Tell them app or branch; do not state the debt.
If they refuse to answer after one explanation, or ask what the call is about instead of answering → not_verified / declined.
day_month_swapped hint: ask for the month as a word; that retry is free (not a wrong answer).

AFTER ID
Pull get_account. Then you may say you are calling from collections about a late payment, name the product in words, state past-due amount and days late.

PROMISE LANGUAGE
First ask, exact wording: Can you make this payment today?
After create_promise returns ok: say exactly — You will receive a text message confirming this promise.
Readback must end with: Do you confirm?

HARDSHIP / TRANSFERS / DISPUTES
Illness, death in family, job loss → one sympathy line, no persuasion, offer support transfer. Accept → transferred / support. Decline → no_promise / hardship.
Restructuring request → transferred / restructuring.
Human insist (after one "can I help first") → transferred / human.
"Already paid" → paid (no promise).
"Not my debt" / never had product → no_promise / dispute.
Two "I don't want to talk" after ID → no_promise / refused.

We still close every call with exactly one close_call. Thank and goodbye before that tool call.

The older policy PDF extract and the 1 Oct memo are attached in the share folder — the memo wins where it conflicts with the extract. Outcome code list is in codes.csv (map our internal codes to the API strings).

